No, I don't want to.

00:23:26.230 --> 00:23:29.970
Well, we do. Take us down, Jimmy. We gotta get...

00:23:30.190 --> 00:23:31.190
Jellyfish home.

00:23:33.820 --> 00:23:34.780
There you go, guys.

00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:37.000
Back to living free and in the wild.

00:23:37.300 --> 00:23:38.100
And forever.

00:23:43.780 --> 00:23:46.720
So there are some animal species that can really

00:23:46.720 --> 00:23:50.740
live for a long, long, long time, like these two.

00:23:51.610 --> 00:23:53.810
This beautiful green-winged macaw

00:23:53.810 --> 00:23:57.370
can live to about 35 to 50 years in the wild,

00:23:57.660 --> 00:23:59.980
and even push about 80 in captivity.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:03.170
And this, Aldabra tortoise.

00:24:03.310 --> 00:24:05.470
This is a youngster, he's already pretty big,

00:24:05.590 --> 00:24:07.330
but only 15 years old.

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:11.510
An Aldabra tortoise can live to be well over 100 years old,

00:24:11.730 --> 00:24:13.410
maybe even 200, maybe 300.

00:24:13.790 --> 00:24:16.130
We don't really even know how long they can live.

00:24:16.620 --> 00:24:19.400
But one thing we know for sure, animals like these,

00:24:19.540 --> 00:24:21.340
they have a lot of birthdays.

00:24:22.550 --> 00:24:23.730
Hey, where you going?

00:24:24.600 --> 00:24:25.800
Oh, tortoise on the move.

00:24:28.110 --> 00:24:29.970
But how long do other animals live?

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:32.980
We've got to talk crustaceans.

00:24:33.120 --> 00:24:36.180
Of all the crustacean species, which live to be the oldest?

00:24:36.820 --> 00:24:37.960
Lobsters get up there.

00:24:38.320 --> 00:24:41.320
A lobster can live over 50 years in the wild.

00:24:41.540 --> 00:24:43.660
And we can't forget about fish.

00:24:43.840 --> 00:24:46.250
What are some of the oldest living fish?

00:24:46.990 --> 00:24:50.790
Female lake sturgeon live to be almost 150 years old.

00:24:51.160 --> 00:24:52.900
Koi, a member of the carp family,

00:24:53.000 --> 00:24:55.320
can live to be more than 200 years old.

00:24:55.870 --> 00:24:56.710
What about insects?

00:24:57.130 --> 00:24:59.970
I never thought about what could be the oldest living fish.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:06.460
insects. And the termite queen could be it. She can live to be over 50 years old. And

00:25:06.460 --> 00:25:13.400
some scientists think she can even get over 100. Now amphibians, what amphibians live

00:25:13.400 --> 00:25:19.010
to be the oldest? Frogs and toads will be lucky to last 15 years in the wild. But remember

00:25:19.010 --> 00:25:25.630
that salamander, the human fish, that can live to be over 100 years old. And then of

00:25:25.630 --> 00:25:29.020
Of course, we can't forget, what are some of the oldest living mammals?

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:32.660
Elephants can live up to 80 years in captivity,

00:25:32.880 --> 00:25:34.680
and over 50 years in the wild.

00:25:35.400 --> 00:25:38.820
But the bowhead whale is the oldest living mammal,

00:25:39.000 --> 00:25:41.660
getting to over 200 years old.

00:25:43.100 --> 00:25:45.340
There are some really special animals

00:25:45.340 --> 00:25:48.260
that live to be over 100 years old.

00:25:48.320 --> 00:25:48.940
Oh, yeah.

00:25:49.380 --> 00:25:51.380
Hey, and keep on creature adventuring.

00:25:51.600 --> 00:25:53.060
We'll see you on the Creature Trail.

00:26:12.120 --> 00:26:17.810
Find out more about cool animals and collect your own Wild Kratz creature powers, go to

00:26:17.810 --> 00:26:21.410
the Wild Kratz website at pbskids.org.

00:26:22.110 --> 00:26:23.130
We'll see you there!
